        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Upper back lump, patient-reported history and symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Patient noticed a little bump approximately 12–18 months ago; it has gradually increased in size and now catches on his high-visibility clothing and work harness. Mild discomfort only when leaning on a hard chair or when the tool belt rubs; otherwise no pain. Patient reports no redness, warmth, discharge, or ulceration."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Upper back skin lesion examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Mid upper back, just left of midline at approximately T4–5: approximately 2.2 cm dome-shaped subcutaneous nodule with normal overlying skin and a small central punctum. Firm and mobile over deeper tissues. Non-tender to light palpation, with mild discomfort on deep pressure. No surrounding erythema, warmth, induration, fluctuance, or discharge."
      }
    },
